.TH POWERGOV-UI 1 "July 2026" "powergov 1.13.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
powergov-ui \- GTK desktop client for the powergov power daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B powergov-ui
.RB [ \-v | \-\-version ]
.RB [ \-h | \-\-help ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B powergov-ui
is a GTK 3 application that controls the
.BR powergov (1)
daemon through the Unix domain socket at
.IR /run/powergov/powergov.sock .
It is intended for laptop users who prefer a graphical interface over the CLI.
.PP
The main window provides:
.TP
.B User
User modes (max-battery, balanced, performance), battery-safe threshold slider,
live status, and optional one-time installation of the systemd backend.
.TP
.B Information
System context (power source, battery, lid state, session idle hint),
compatibility notes (TLP, power-profiles-daemon), metrics and log viewers,
feature toggles, custom-mode tuning, and context options (lid/display aggression).
.TP
.B About
Version strings for UI and daemon (same format as
.BR "powergov \-v" ),
GPLv3 notice, and project link.
.PP
Closing the window with the title-bar
.B X
hides the application to the **system tray** (lightning icon) unless
.B POWERGOV_NO_TRAY=1
is set, in which case
.B X
exits the process.
.PP
Optional feature and tuning checkboxes use an **optimistic pending** state:
the UI reflects the user's choice immediately while the daemon applies and
confirms the change asynchronously.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-v
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print version and licensing banner, then exit.
.TP
.B \-h
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print brief usage and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B POWERGOV_NO_TRAY=1
Disable system tray; closing the window terminates the UI.
.TP
.B POWERGOV_FG=1
Run in foreground (used by AppImage / desktop entry).
.TP
.B LANG
.B LC_MESSAGES
.B LANGUAGE
If any starts with
.BR es ,
the UI defaults to Spanish; otherwise English. An EN/ES toggle is available
in the title bar.
.TP
.B PG_UPDATE_CHECK_DELAY_MS
Milliseconds before checking GitHub Releases for updates (default 5000).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /run/powergov/powergov.sock
Control socket shared with
.BR powergov (1) .
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/powergov/PowerGov.AppImage
Stable install path used by the AppImage updater.
.TP
.I /usr/local/share/applications/powergov-ui.desktop
Desktop entry when installed from source.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
The
.B powergov
daemon must be running (typically
.BR "systemctl start powergov" ).
Without the daemon, the UI can offer to install or start the service (Polkit
prompt for administrator password).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Run from a source build:
.RS
.B ./powergov-ui
.RE
.TP
Spanish locale:
.RS
.B LANG=es_ES.UTF-8 powergov-ui
.RE
.TP
No system tray:
.RS
.B POWERGOV_NO_TRAY=1 powergov-ui
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR powergov (1),
.BR powergov (8),
.BR powergov.conf (5),
.IR ui/README.md
in the source tree.
